# Sparse SAE codes as a representation, mirroring two dense readouts so the
# sparsity question is a controlled contrast:
#
#   sae_last  <-> last_token    the step's final token, raw state vs sparse code
#   sae_mean  <-> step_mean     mean over the step's tokens, likewise
#
# Same layer, same activations, same trainer, same hyperparameter protocol.
# Qwen-Scope TopK, 65,536 features, k=50, reconstruction FVU 0.336 at this layer.
#
# The prediction is that these LOSE. The SAE discards a third of the variance,
# and section 15 found step correctness to be a distributed low-variance margin,
# which is exactly what a dictionary trained for reconstruction has no reason to
# keep. A clean loss is informative; a win would be more so.

sae_last linear
sae_last mlp:h1024
sae_mean linear
sae_mean mlp:h1024
